Product goal (user, 2026-11-14 14:58): an assistive proofreader that does the fine-print reading before an admin looks at an edit. Maximise, in priority order: (1) accuracy — flag only concerning changes; false positives/negatives destroy admin trust and add rework; (2) efficiency — latency scales with edit size, low upper bound (never minutes for a one-line change); (3) resource usage — low CPU and tokens; prompts/harness/context must not bloat. Balance all three; never trade one away in a major way.
